  "compatibility_policy": {
    "unknown_tag": "SKIP the frame and keep the session alive. Never ERR, never close. A tag this build does not know is a producer speaking a newer revision, not a corrupt stream.",
    "tag_registry": "APPEND-ONLY. A tag number, once published in TAGS, is frozen to its meaning forever; it may never be reused or renumbered. Adding a tag is NOT a breaking change (see unknown_tag) \u2014 renumbering one is, and it is the change no consumer can detect. This is the D.14 rule.",
    "unknown_key": "IGNORE it. Adding an optional map key to an existing frame is additive and non-breaking. A consumer MUST NOT fail on a key it does not know, so the required-key set below is the whole of what a consumer may rely on.",
    "unknown_enum_member": "FALL BACK to the documented default for that field (channel `type` -> Signal, `role` -> Wire, `radix` -> Hexadecimal). This is what RouteWave already does, so a producer that invents a member gets SILENT fallback -- which is why unregistered members are a contract violation on the PRODUCER side even though they are survivable on the consumer side.",
    "unknown_kind": "RENDER it generically. Annotation `kind` is a free-form producer string; a consumer groups and filters on it but never interprets it. A kind REGISTERED in ANNOTATION_PAYLOAD below must carry its registered role keys \u2014 that key set is the cross-repo contract.",
    "body_schema": "SKIP the frame. A frame that carries its own body-schema string (DIGEST) versions its body independently of the wire tag; a consumer that does not implement the body revision skips that frame only.",
    "version_mismatch": "FATAL, and the only fatal incompatibility. A HELO.ver whose value this side does not implement ends the session: answer ERR {code: VERSION_MISMATCH} and close. Guessing at an unknown wire version is how a green session stops meaning what it says."
  },
